        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(diagnostics): expose zero-output context pressure",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nLong-running sessions can terminate a model call with explicit zero output or zero tool calls as context pressure reaches the effective window. OpenClaw's diagnostics dropped those zero values, so operators could not distinguish a real zero-output terminal call from missing telemetry.\n\nFixes #100113.\n\nRelated recovery work: #100042 and #100077.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Preserve explicit zero token and tool-call values in model-call and aggregate OTEL spans.\n- Add sanitized terminal facts: stop reason, content-block count, tool-call count, effective-window overflow detection, and prompt utilization.\n- Keep overflow telemetry identical to the runtime recovery classifier.\n- Derive Codex overflow only from unambiguous completed-turn evidence; omit ambiguous values instead of reporting false.\n- Project Codex usage and terminal facts from its app-server result, including tool counts from canonical projected turn items.\n- Keep absent usage absent rather than synthesizing zero.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOTEL traces can now identify the failure signature behind zero-output/tool-call turns near context exhaustion without capturing model content. This improves diagnosis of long-session context failures without changing retries, compaction, provider routing, configuration, or persisted state.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact pushed head: `371fb6b32f9955fa10f3f71b6c65be2cbc211b6d`.\n- Final autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Crabbox/Testbox `tbx_01kx72g7w4gwn0zqp8xxyw5d7d`:\n  - exact-head focused proof: 29 tests passed across embedded model-call and Codex diagnostics\n  - path-scoped `check:changed` proof passed core/extension typechecks, test typechecks, docs, lint, guards, and import-cycle checks\n- `oxfmt --check` passed for touched follow-up files.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- The final conflict-free rebase preserved the validated patch byte-for-byte (`sha256:7da3d67ddea600584878a3de022ee18e850cecfca0d798a8ad59118fe60cf540`).\n- Direct upstream Codex source checked for token-usage events, canonical command/MCP/dynamic tool-call items, turn completion, and terminal error propagation.\n\nThe unscoped delegated changed gate was also attempted, but a full-sync rebase made the wrapper classify thousands of upstream files as changed and fail on generated shrinkwrap state. The path-scoped changed gate above ran the actual affected lanes successfully on the same Testbox lease.\n",
        "branch": "investigate/tool-call-zero-context",
